  "title": "Mariam al-Astrulabi (al-Ijliyya)",
  "summary": "Called Mariam al-Astrulabi or al-Ijliyya in modern accounts, she was a tenth-century astrolabe maker in Aleppo. Sources say she learned from her father, whose own teacher was a maker in Baghdad, and that Sayf al-Dawla, who ruled Aleppo from 944 to 967, employed her at his court. Her birth and death dates are not recorded.",
